= render 'shared/support_page', page_title: 'Asking for Help', current_page: 'Asking for Help', parent_page: true, page_subtitle: 'Get answers quicker with this handy checklist', document_title: 'Asking for Help Checklist', meta: ['Pixel troubleshooting', 'FPP & xLights', 'What to include'], toc: support_asking_for_help_toc do
  p.lead If you're reading this, someone has sent you this link to help you get answers quicker. With showtime looming it can be stressful when things go wrong — run through this checklist first.

  .prose.support-prose
    section#pixels-wrong.check-card
      h2
        span.hk
          span.bar
          span.annot Pixels
        | If the pixels are not doing what they should

      p This is usually a channel overlap issue and easily sortable.

      .callout.warn
        span.ic
          svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"
            path d="M10.3 3.9 1.8 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.7 3h17a2 2 0 0 0 1.7-3L13.7 3.9a2 2 0 0 0-3.4 0z"
        div
          span.lbl Important
          p.bd
            | Make sure each of your controllers has Auto Layout Models and Auto Layout Size and, if possible, full xLights Control enabled.
            em  If you cannot do that, make sure all your controllers have separate channels and universes.

      .steps
        .step Re-render the sequence
        .step In xLights on the controller tab, click "output to lights" on each of your controllers and keep an eye on the bottom left that they all succeed (sometimes they can fail)
        .step
          | Then in xLights click FPP Connect and do an upload with
          strong  UDP Out
          |  set to
          em  ALL
          |  on your main show controller
        .step
          | Check that the channels in xLights match the channels in FPP and on the
          = link_to ' Baldrick8', board_path('baldrick8'), class: 'lnk'
          |  controller

    section#fpp-output.check-card
      h2
        span.hk
          span.bar
          span.annot FPP
        | If the pixels are not outputting via FPP

      .steps
        .step
          | Make sure test mode isn't enabled on the
          = link_to ' Baldrick8', board_path('baldrick8'), class: 'lnk'
        .step Check the E1.31 Outputs tab in FPP and ensure the IP address matches your controller IP address
        .step Check the E1.31 Outputs tab in FPP and ensure the channels match the ones in the xLights controller tab
        .step
          | Enable test mode on FPP and look at the stats box on the
          = link_to ' Baldrick8', board_path('baldrick8'), class: 'lnk'
          |  — is it receiving data?

    section#xlights-output.check-card
      h2
        span.hk
          span.bar
          span.annot xLights
        | If the pixels are not outputting via xLights

      .steps
        .step
          | Make sure test mode isn't enabled on the
          = link_to ' Baldrick8', board_path('baldrick8'), class: 'lnk'
        .step Check the controller tab in xLights and ensure the IP address matches your controller IP address
        .step Push outputs to the controller and make sure it's successful
        .step Enable test mode on FPP and look at the stats box on the Baldrick8 — is it receiving data?

    section#still-stuck.check-card.check-card--warn
      h2
        span.hk
          span.bar
          span.annot Escalate
        | That didn't help

      p
        | If the checklist didn't solve it, it's time to ask for help. If you are going to post on the
        = link_to ' Baldrick community Facebook group', t('facebook_group_url'), target: '_blank', rel: 'noopener', class: 'lnk'
        | , include the following — you'll almost certainly be asked for them anyway:

      .rn-subcard
        h4 Essential information to include
        ul
          li
            strong What is the issue you are having
            |  (be as detailed as possible)
          li
            strong What have you tried so far
          li
            strong
              | What version of xLights, FPP and/or
              = link_to ' Baldrick8', board_path('baldrick8'), class: 'lnk'
              |  firmware
            |  are you using
          li
            strong Please include screenshots
            |  of your xLights controller tab (with the
            = link_to ' Baldrick8', board_path('baldrick8'), class: 'lnk'
            |  selected), your FPP E1.31 Outputs page and your xLights Models section
          li
            strong If possible, a photo of the controller
            |  wired up
          li
            strong A bit of info about your network setup!

      .callout.warn
        span.ic
          svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"
            path d="M10.3 3.9 1.8 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.7 3h17a2 2 0 0 0 1.7-3L13.7 3.9a2 2 0 0 0-3.4 0z"
        div
          span.lbl Pro tip
          p.bd These might seem like a pain to gather, but trust us — it will get you a solution quicker. There is no such thing as too much information.

      .next-grid
        = link_to t('facebook_group_url'), class: 'next-card', target: '_blank', rel: 'noopener' do
          .top
            span.kind Community
            span.go →
          h4 Facebook group
          p Post your question with all the information above for the fastest response.
        = link_to support_path, class: 'next-card' do
          .top
            span.kind Hardware
            span.go →
          h4 Hardware support
          p Physical defects or warranty claims — open a triage case.

section.cta
  .wrap
    h2 Still wiring things up?
    p Board manuals cover setup, web interface and troubleshooting per controller.
    .cta-btns
      = link_to boards_path, class: 'btn btn-bone' do
        | Board manuals
        span.ar →
      = link_to fun_stuff_faq_path, class: 'btn btn-clear' do
        | General FAQ
